  "hypotheses": [
    "Worker synchronization/oversubscription: default four CPU threads on the recorded three-CPU VM predicts graph/barrier waiting with pool recreation absent. Source and counts alone do not prove the remaining cost.",
    "Arithmetic: matrix/convolution/Accelerate paths may dominate sampled worker activity even with an owned pool.",
    "Shared-VM scheduling pressure: load and process CPU/wall accounting may show pressure; stack samples alone cannot isolate scheduler causality."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Exactly one fresh 12s public C ABI neural process after a successful model-free sampling control. Reuse immutable M1-built pool-v1 package, qualified executable and saved independent pooled12s reference. No private C++ layout access, old helper reuse, thread/poll/geometry/weight/default change or native SDK build.",
    "Bind complete delivery ZIPs, metadata, all members, package/helpers/assets inventories, actual normalized PCM and all1200x8 finite probabilities/turns. Require exact pool-v1 identities before unchanged1e-6 mathematical comparison. Report byte equality separately. Child cannot read reference/source/prior-output data, write protected inputs or use network; strict native92-image and controlzero-image audits remain.",
    "Sample requested five seconds using live traced PID/executable and exact dyld/report UUID; actual report may be shorter if the process ends. Deliver both sampled executables for independent hash checks. Retain time/RSS, CPU counts, load, output arrays and failure evidence. No automatic retry; original5GiB/1GiB/256MiB/600s process-group protections remain.",
    "This is descriptive shared-VM sampling, not an uncontended throughput/speedup comparison or causal scheduler proof. No production policy selection, held-out quality, human timing gold, GUI/microphone, portable app delivery, public signing or release qualification. Original failed gates stay open."
  ]
